// Feature 9: XStore association mapping -- cross-store join expressed as a predicate.
// Source: legend-engine TestMappingGrammarRoundtrip#testCrossStoreAssociationMapping
//         (legend-engine-language-pure-grammar .../roundtrip/TestMappingGrammarRoundtrip.java:820)
// Exact spelling:
//   * the association body is `XStore { ... }` (no AssociationMapping(...) wrapper,
//     unlike the Relational form)
//   * each end is `prop[sourceSetId, targetSetId]: <boolean expression>`; the set ids
//     are optional, exactly as in the Relational form
//   * the predicate uses `$this` (source side) and `$that` (target side).
//     There is NO `~target` keyword anywhere in legend-engine.
//   * `~src <Class>` belongs to the M2M (`Pure`) CLASS mappings, not to the XStore block
//   * `+firmId: Integer[1]: 1` is a LOCAL mapping property -- it is not on demo::Person;
//     it exists only to give the XStore predicate a join key.
###Pure
Class demo::Person
{
  name: String[1];
}

Class demo::Firm
{
  id: Integer[1];
  legalName: String[1];
}

Association demo::Firm_Person
{
  employer: demo::Firm[1];
  employees: demo::Person[*];
}

###Mapping
Mapping demo::CrossStoreMapping
(
  demo::Person[p]: Pure
  {
    ~src demo::Person
    +firmId: Integer[1]: 1,
    name: $src.name
  }

  demo::Firm[f]: Pure
  {
    ~src demo::Firm
    id: $src.id,
    legalName: $src.legalName
  }

  demo::Firm_Person: XStore
  {
    employer[p, f]: $this.firmId == $that.id,
    employees[f, p]: $this.id == $that.firmId
  }
)
